-- Equilibration with two PVT regions in a compositional run.  A column of 20
-- cells is split into two blocks of ten, each its own equilibration region and
-- PVT region, with a water zone at its base.  The upper block holds fresh water
-- (region 1, 1000 kg/m3 at surface) and the lower block brine (region 2, 1150
-- kg/m3 at surface).  Layer 10 has no vertical permeability, so no fluid
-- crosses between the blocks.
--
-- The water zone of each block is equilibrated with the water of its own PVT
-- region.  The pressure in the lower water zone rises with the brine density,
-- about 1141 kg/m3, and both blocks stay at rest.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   COMPOSITIONAL EQUILIBRATION OVER TWO PVT REGIONS

METRIC

TABDIMS
1* 2 /
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
1 1 20 /

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

EQLDIMS
2 200 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INIT

GRIDFILE
0 1 /

DX
20*5 /
DY
20*100 /
DZ
20*5 /
TOPS
1*2000.0 /
PORO
20*0.3 /
PERMX
20*2000 /
PERMY
20*2000 /
-- Layer 10 has no vertical permeability, which cuts it off from layers 9 and
-- 11 alike: no flow crosses between the upper and the lower block, and each
-- stays in its own hydrostatic equilibrium.
PERMZ
9*2000 0 10*2000 /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/PROPS.inc' /

-- One record per PVT region.
ROCK
    68.9476  0.0 /
    68.9476  0.0 /

PVTW
    75.0  1.03  4.0E-5  0.3  0.0 /
    75.0  1.01  2.5E-5  0.9  0.0 /

DENSITY
    800.0  1000.0  1.0 /
    800.0  1150.0  1.0 /

ZMFVD
 2000   0 0.7 0.3
 2100   0 0.3 0.7  /
 2000   0 0.7 0.3
 2100   0 0.3 0.7  /

RTEMP
100
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
EQLNUM
10*1 10*2
/
PVTNUM
10*1 10*2
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The water-oil contact of each block lies three layers above its base.
EQUIL
   2010  250  2035  0  2000  0  /
   2060  155  2085  0  2050  0  /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
ALL

-- Block values at the top of each block and in its water zone.
BPR
1 1 1 /
1 1 9 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 19 /
1 1 20 /
/

BGSAT
1 1 1 /
1 1 9 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 19 /
1 1 20 /
/

BOSAT
1 1 1 /
1 1 9 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 19 /
1 1 20 /
/

BWSAT
1 1 1 /
1 1 9 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 19 /
1 1 20 /
/

BDENW
1 1 1 /
1 1 9 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 19 /
1 1 20 /
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHEDULE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INCLUDE
 'include/REPORTING.inc' /

TSTEP
0.01 0.02 0.1 0.2 1.0 5.0
/
END
